<title>GERMANY: Bundesbank sets tender for 13-day repos at 3 pct.</title>
<headline>Bundesbank sets tender for 13-day repos at 3 pct.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-12-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bundesbank said on Monday it was setting a tender for 13-day securities repurchase funds, offering banks liquidity at a fixed rate of 3.00 percent.</p>
<p>A 83.4 billion-mark repo pact expires on Thursday. The repo rates has been fixed at 3.00 percent since late August.</p>
<p>The repo tenders are usually set on Tuesdays with allocations following on Wednesdays but the dates have been changed this week because of the Christmas and New Year holidays.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom + 49 69 756525</p>
